-- title:
--   Two prolongations exhaust the pencil line over X₀(q)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A \to k$. Let `data` be modular polynomial data for $q$ (a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb Z[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ annihilating the $q$-expansion pair of $j$), let `hKr` assert the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \equiv (X^q - Y)(X - Y^q)$ modulo $q$, and let `hα`, `hβ` assert that the level-one Hecke maps $\overline{\alpha}$, $\overline{\beta}$ for $q$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ are integral ring homomorphisms. Let $P$ be a place specialization of this data and $R$ a level-one prolongation pair for $P$; in particular $R$ provides two regular prolongations $R_1$, $R_2$ of $A$ to $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, each consisting of a valuation subring of $F$ whose intersection with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $A$, together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto the level-one full modular function field over the residue field of $A$ with kernel the maximal ideal, the two being interchanged by the Fricke involution. Let $\mu \in A$ satisfy $\mathrm{red}(\mu) \neq 0$, and let $O$ be a valuation subring of $F$ agreeing with the integers of $R_1$ on the subfield $\overline{\mathbb Q}(j + \mu\, j_q)$ generated by `jFun` $+\ \mu\cdot$ `jqFun`, i.e. $x \in O \iff x \in R_1$.`integers` for every $x$ in that intermediate field. Then $O$ equals the integers of $R_1$ or the integers of $R_2$.
--
--   This is the exhaustiveness statement for the pencil line: the two prolongations of $A$ furnished by a level-one prolongation pair are the only valuation rings of the function field of $X_0(q)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose restriction to $\overline{\mathbb Q}(j + \mu j_q)$ is the one cut out by $R_1$, the hypothesis $\mathrm{red}(\mu) \neq 0$ being what makes the degree count $q + q \le 2q$ tight. It is used in [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.LevelOneProlongationPair.sum_filter_value_eq_sum_roots_add_pencil`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.LevelOneProlongationPair.sum_filter_value_eq_sum_roots_add_pencil), within the analysis of the reduction of $X_0(q)$ governed by the Kronecker congruence.
